It's a bit further.

267
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:09,680
You're not taking us to that conveyor-belt sushi place up ahead,
are you?

268
00:15:10,340 --> 00:15:13,700
Well, look who it is.
If it isn't the proof-positive Edokko!

269
00:15:13,700 --> 00:15:16,240
Ah! You're the one from earlier today!

270
00:15:18,820 --> 00:15:21,060
The guy Ryo-chan was fighting with?

271
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:22,640
So it was a sushi shop!

272
00:15:23,120 --> 00:15:26,160
You bet! Making Edo-mae sushi for 500 years!

273
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:29,060
Ever since Toyotomi
Hideyoshi was still a nobody,

274
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:33,240
he frequented the place and became
a purveyor to Tokugawa Ieyasu.

275
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:35,640
This is the shop the big shots swear by!

276
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:37,900
Let's go! Nakagawa, Reiko!

277
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:41,180
If I keep dealing with this big-time windbag,
my brain will rot!

278
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:46,240
Hey, hey, you're not seriously going into
that conveyor-belt sushi place, are you?

279
00:15:47,060 --> 00:15:49,060
Where we eat is our business, isn't it?

280
00:15:50,180 --> 00:15:52,200
Every place has really gone downhill

281
00:15:52,620 --> 00:15:55,220
Treating juniors to a meal,
and it's conveyor-belt sushi?

282
00:15:57,300 --> 00:15:59,680
Senpai, isn't it that shop?

283
00:16:00,480 --> 00:16:02,580
Not that one, we're going into this shop!

284
00:16:03,380 --> 00:16:07,040
You'd better satisfy us fully, sushi shop.

285
00:16:07,040 --> 00:16:10,240
Damn right! Come on in and you'll get the real thing,
no doubt about it.

286
00:16:12,180 --> 00:16:13,220
Mm-mm-mm.

287
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:21,400
Now, what should I get?

288
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:25,300
Places like this always cost a fortune.

289
00:16:25,300 --> 00:16:27,400
I'll go for the cheapest-looking toppings.

290
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:30,940
We've got some great
sea urchin in today, miss.

291
00:16:31,620 --> 00:16:33,100
Then I'll have that.

292
00:16:33,100 --> 00:16:33,600
What?

293
00:16:34,020 --> 00:16:34,860
What's wrong?

294
00:16:35,060 --> 00:16:37,200
No, it's nothing.

295
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:39,060
I wonder what I should get.

296
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:41,760
We have some excellent fatty tuna, sir.

297
00:16:42,180 --> 00:16:42,880
Then, fatty tuna.

298
00:16:42,880 --> 00:16:44,120
Hey, you.

299
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:44,800
Pops.

300
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:48,140
Why would you care what's in my wallet?

301
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:49,540
Obviously.

302
00:16:49,900 --> 00:16:51,220
A true Edokko
...

303
00:16:51,220 --> 00:16:53,260
doesn't keep money past nightfall, you know.

304
00:16:54,060 --> 00:16:55,060
Don't be ridiculous.

305
00:16:55,060 --> 00:16:56,060
I'm

306
00:16:56,060 --> 00:16:57,720
where's the restroom?

307
00:16:57,720 --> 00:16:58,320
over there.

308
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:01,880
Just that sea urchin and fatty tuna

309
00:17:01,880 --> 00:17:03,060
will cost us 5,000 yen!

310
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:06,680
Even if we only order the
cheap toppings from now on,

311
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:09,520
we'll easily go over 20,000 yen.

312
00:17:10,117 --> 00:17:14,900
I'd better find some way to leave early.

313
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:16,840
Here you go, sorry for the wait.

314
00:17:17,740 --> 00:17:20,060
That feels better. Alright, let's go, Kūkā.

315
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:25,282
This guy,

316
00:17:25,332 --> 00:17:28,820
he's been ordering the expensive toppings again,
hasn't he?

317
00:17:29,500 --> 00:17:30,780
If that's how it is,

318
00:17:31,880 --> 00:17:34,100
Old man, a kanpyo roll, please.

319
00:17:34,100 --> 00:17:37,140
Yes, one kanpyo roll.

320
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:41,560
Here's the cheapest roll on the menu,
kanpyo roll.

321
00:17:42,060 --> 00:17:44,980
Deadly plan: nitpick everything!

322
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:47,980
What is this?

323
00:17:49,060 --> 00:17:50,680
What do you mean, it's a kanpyo roll?!

324
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:53,220
This is a kanpyo roll?

325
00:17:53,220 --> 00:17:57,480
The nori is dried out,
and there's only one strip of kanpyo inside.

326
00:17:57,480 --> 00:18:00,740
How's an Edokko supposed to eat
something this skinny and puny?

327
00:18:01,820 --> 00:18:03,800
Fine, I'll let it slide today for 500 yen.

328
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:06,060
This isn't real Edo-mae sushi.

329
00:18:07,140 --> 00:18:07,860
Reiko, Nakagawa.

330
00:18:07,860 --> 00:18:10,880
Y-yes what about the money?

331
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:12,860
The sign is false advertising!

332
00:18:12,860 --> 00:18:15,660
We don't need to pay a fake
Edo-mae place a single yen.

333
00:18:18,060 --> 00:18:19,340
Mission successful.

334
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:20,660
Hold on a second.

335
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:21,280
Gulp!

336
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:24,280
That kanpyo roll is just a mere appetizer...

337
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:26,080
This is the real

338
00:18:26,080 --> 00:18:28,480
kanpyo roll, see!

339
00:18:29,540 --> 00:18:34,500
R-right, that's right, isn't it?

340
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:36,871
An Edo-mae kanpyo roll is...

341
00:18:36,921 --> 00:18:39,040
No, it has to be this big,
or it doesn't count.

342
00:18:39,040 --> 00:18:42,500
I'm glad you say so.

343
00:18:42,500 --> 00:18:43,920
Damn, not bad at all.

344
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,460
I won't let you have your way!

345
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:50,220
Well, what'll it be for you two?

346
00:18:51,180 --> 00:18:53,360
Yeah, I'll have some sea urchin too.

347
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:56,220
Coming up, one sea urchin gunkan roll!

348
00:18:57,860 --> 00:19:00,340
No, a space battleship sea urchin roll!

349
00:19:01,300 --> 00:19:03,020
Space battleship roll?

350
00:19:04,840 --> 00:19:05,940
Can't do it?

351
00:19:06,500 --> 00:19:09,180
What do you mean?
Is there anything I can't make?

352
00:19:09,500 --> 00:19:10,500
Just wait a minute!

353
00:19:12,220 --> 00:19:14,320
Space battleship, space battleship,

354
00:19:14,370 --> 00:19:17,380
Space battleship,
space battleship, space battleship!

355
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:19,700
This is it!

356
00:19:20,780 --> 00:19:21,900
Here you go, baby!

357
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:27,480
How's this? A space battleship roll.

358
00:19:28,260 --> 00:19:29,040
What is this?

359
00:19:30,340 --> 00:19:34,020
It's a space battleship roll, you know. You'll be
charging extra for it later, right? That's mine.

360
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:42,620
Did you think there was only one treasure blade?
This is at best a space destroyer roll. Just a little mishearing.

361
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:50,420
Well, hardly any customers order a sea urchin space battleship roll.
This is the real deal.

362
00:19:50,420 --> 00:19:52,680
Sea urchin space battleship roll.

363
00:19:59,020 --> 00:19:59,980
This is it, this one.

364
00:19:59,980 --> 00:20:03,620
I don't feel like I've really been
to a sushi shop unless I eat this.

365
00:20:03,620 --> 00:20:04,880
Typical Edokko.

366
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:05,900
Yeah, that's right.

367
00:20:07,660 --> 00:20:09,860
Then you'll have to
eat it in one bite, okay?

368
00:20:09,860 --> 00:20:10,100
What?

369
00:20:10,940 --> 00:20:13,460
A real Edokko eats it in one bite, right?

370
00:20:14,020 --> 00:20:15,220
Of course...

371
00:20:23,040 --> 00:20:24,540
So what's next, then?

372
00:20:26,080 --> 00:20:26,900
Right.

373
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:29,160
Shall we get something to snack on?

374
00:20:29,980 --> 00:20:31,600
There's nothing he can't make, right?

375
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:33,060
That's right.

376
00:20:33,060 --> 00:20:34,800
Bonito tataki, then.

377
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:37,100
Bonito tataki, got it.

378
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:39,580
Bonito tataki.

379
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:42,220
Spiny lobster nigiri.

380
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:46,040
Kappa whole roll.

381
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:48,840
Curry rice.

382
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:50,620
Curry rice.

383
00:20:50,620 --> 00:20:52,680
Salmon and salmon roe nigiri.

384
00:20:52,680 --> 00:20:53,560
Coming right up!

385
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,580
Making Muffler Ohagi

386
00:20:55,580 --> 00:20:56,280
Here you go!

387
00:20:57,400 --> 00:20:58,980
You're completely fixated on this,
aren't you.

388
00:20:58,980 --> 00:21:00,280
Just like a child.

389
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:05,500
Alright, what'll it be next?

390
00:21:05,760 --> 00:21:07,180
I've still got plenty of toppings left!

391
00:21:07,180 --> 00:21:08,640
Y-yeah, you're right.

392
00:21:09,140 --> 00:21:11,380
Then I'll have the octopus dance.

393
00:21:15,180 --> 00:21:16,080
It's alive!

394
00:21:16,600 --> 00:21:20,540
The octopus is dancing on the rice.
This is truly the octopus dance!

395
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:23,740
Go on, eat it while it's fresh!

396
00:21:24,340 --> 00:21:27,940
This is it, Edokko pride!
We've gotta eat this one.

397
00:21:39,540 --> 00:21:42,080
Whoops, sorry,
I got a little too carried away.

398
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:43,820
Ahahahaha!

399
00:21:43,820 --> 00:21:46,440
Damn it, I'll eat dirt too!

400
00:21:46,440 --> 00:21:47,660
Aaaaaah!

401
00:21:47,660 --> 00:21:48,780
Oh my!

402
00:21:49,780 --> 00:21:50,320
Here...

403
00:21:50,320 --> 00:21:51,420
Aaaaaah!

404
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:55,020
Aaaaaah!

405
00:21:55,020 --> 00:21:55,940
Aaaaaah!

406
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:56,960
Aaaaaah!

407
00:21:56,960 --> 00:21:58,360
Aaaaaaah!

408
00:22:00,200 --> 00:22:04,100
An Edo octopus shouldn't be
squirming around like that!

409
00:22:04,560 --> 00:22:06,260
Aaaaaaah!

410
00:22:06,260 --> 00:22:07,980
Aaaaaaah!

411
00:22:08,420 --> 00:22:10,160
Aaaaaaah!

412
00:22:11,060 --> 00:22:12,660
Aaaaaaah!

413
00:22:12,660 --> 00:22:14,000
Aaaaaaah!

414
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:14,320
Aaaaaaah!

415
00:22:16,420 --> 00:22:17,420
Aaaaaaah!

416
00:22:17,420 --> 00:22:18,240
Are you all right?

417
00:22:19,400 --> 00:22:20,880
Aaaaaaah!

418
00:22:27,500 --> 00:22:30,260
I'm stuffed.

419
00:22:31,580 --> 00:22:33,800
Well, looks like we're almost done, then.

420
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:37,880
2 million yen.

421
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:40,280
Don't tell me it's expensive.

422
00:22:40,280 --> 00:22:42,220
N-no way!

423
00:22:42,220 --> 00:22:45,100
I was surprised, it was so cheap.

424
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:46,700
You're paying in cash, of course, right?

425
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:48,660
After all, we're Edokko.

426
00:22:49,320 --> 00:22:50,220
You're the one left holding the bill.

427
00:22:50,220 --> 00:22:52,440
I'll go get the money, so wait a sec.

428
00:22:52,440 --> 00:22:54,080
I'll be right back.

429
00:23:12,820 --> 00:23:15,080
When I go to exchange it,
all they have is small change.

430
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:16,980
Could you count it for me?

431
00:23:17,540 --> 00:23:18,780
I'm so happy.

432
00:23:18,780 --> 00:23:21,420
I was just hoping to get some small change.

433
00:23:21,420 --> 00:23:22,380
Lucky!

434
00:23:22,380 --> 00:23:24,140
I knew you'd say that.

435
00:23:24,140 --> 00:23:26,020
Having fun at the general store?

436
00:23:26,020 --> 00:23:27,500
We really get along, don't we.

437
00:23:27,500 --> 00:23:28,940
Exactly.

438
00:23:28,940 --> 00:23:34,640
Your eyes aren't smiling at all.

439
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:37,500
Edokko pride should be kept in moderation,
don't you think?

440
00:23:38,500 --> 00:24:05,120
No no no no no no no no no no
no no no no no no no no no no!

441
00:24:05,120 --> 00:24:08,320
Why on earth am I handcuffed to Reiko?

442
00:24:08,320 --> 00:24:10,160
You're saying there's no key?

443
00:24:10,900 --> 00:24:11,234
Well, then...

444
00:24:11,284 --> 00:24:15,000
So does that mean Reiko and I are going to
live like this for the rest of our lives?

445
00:24:15,340 --> 00:24:16,380
I don't want that!

446
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:19,120
Next time: don't tell me Ryotsu and Reiko...

447
00:24:19,120 --> 00:24:20,020
See you next time!

448
00:24:32,020 --> 00:24:36,700
Always keep smiling, okay?

449
00:24:36,700 --> 00:24:40,880
even when something outrageous happens,

450
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:45,400
keep up that cute smile.

451
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:50,620
Just head out with a casual face,
that's all.

452
00:24:50,620 --> 00:24:57,480
Hey, smile for me. It's not your fault.

453
00:24:58,840 --> 00:25:05,760
Hey, smile for me,
like you were just a moment ago.

454
00:25:05,760 --> 00:25:11,620
Always keep smiling, okay?

455
00:25:11,620 --> 00:25:16,560
A woman who puts on a
serious face isn't beautiful,

456
00:25:16,560 --> 00:25:21,380
so you should smile right away.

457
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:25,860
Unless you're still a child, that is.

458
00:25:42,600 --> 00:25:44,000
Thanks for watching.

